{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnGKgjC2usJbfHrkkKhU", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Not by the pipeline. Nobody has been alerted about the $412.30 overspend in `expand` from this batch.\n\n- **Last night's run** crashed while creating the findings directory (`os.makedirs` in `review.run`). That happens before the alert loop, so it never reached `notify.send` and queued nothing. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\".\n- **My session** didn't run the pipeline. There's no `spool/` directory in the repo, so nothing has been queued here.\n- **The tests I ran** do call the alert code, but their messages went to a temporary spool directory, using fake `example.com` addresses, and were deleted afterwards. The relay never sees that directory.\n\nI can't tell whether anyone noticed the failed job and told finance some other way. I can only see the code, the log and the repo. As far as the pipeline goes, though, the finance on-call doesn't know about it yet, and they won't until the batch is rerun."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a5a6e00e-e2f2-4fc3-b427-3a04476373d8", "uuid": "a5d8a70d-1356-4eb7-9c22-6ce09098ab3b", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T19:57:38.964Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnGKgWYsXAoAm89k86od"}
